@@ -18,6 +18,18 @@ Every validated change appends immutable asset, theme, or collection records. **
 
 An edited pixel document must be prepared or explicitly discarded. A prepared upload must be staged or explicitly discarded before switching assets or saving. Browser navigation warns about prepared or staged work. A second tab cannot silently overwrite a newer local generation: a stale save fails and keeps the in-memory workspace available for export. Export it before resetting/reloading. If IndexedDB is unavailable or corrupt, the default inventory still works in memory and remains exportable; saving stays blocked until a successful reload. No repair action clears player or Studio storage automatically.
 
+## Explicit reference workspace upgrade
+
+The source candidate supports v1 inline and v2 reference workspaces. The workspace summary identifies the loaded format. Ordinary load, edits and Save retain that format. Export a v1 backup with **Export .rltheme** before choosing **Upgrade workspace to v2**. The upgrade preserves every historical record and original payload, changes only the envelope and its revision, and stages an unsaved draft. **Undo draft** or **Reset to saved** restores v1 before Save. Save persists v2 through the same generation check; older Studios then refuse it and cannot overwrite it with a v1 draft. Later v2 edits cannot be downgraded into a v1 export by discarding history.
+
+v2 revisions may refer to a hash-checked inline provenance anchor within the same workspace. History, prompts, coverage and previews resolve the actual creator, license and brief; they never expose an unresolved anchor as user content. Asset edits, review records, tokens, theme selection, historical binding and complete collection replacement all append immutable records. A v2 workspace can import a verified v1 or v2 collection. A v1 workspace refuses v2 imports with explicit upgrade guidance; importing or loading a release collection never upgrades an existing workspace silently.
+
+The limits stay at 4 MiB for the encoded manifest and transfer metadata, 32 MiB for the full transfer and 2,048 asset records. Original bytes and shared file facts remain verified. Export may refuse a document whose extra transfer table exceeds its budget; a saveable document is not a promise of unlimited portable history. The producer and default compiler CLI remain v1 in this candidate; no production ledger is migrated.
+
+**Cancel** before a staged operation finishes leaves its previous draft intact. **Stop waiting** during Save does not promise rollback and keeps changes locked until the save settles. Terminal departure closes this Studio's owned connection and aborts its pending v2 transaction when still abortable; a transaction already committed remains committed. Persisted navigation leaves the connection usable, and the next save still checks the actual generation. This follows [IndexedDB transaction abort semantics](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IDBTransaction/abort). Upgrade hands its own foreground focus to Save after unlocking; deliberate newer focus is retained. The existing guide is a disclosure, not a new modal. Any later modal must follow [W3C dialog focus and Escape guidance](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/dialog-modal/).
+
+Focused source tests exercise the real Studio handlers with finite DOM/storage/image fixtures. They do not establish real-browser migration, native image decoding, two-tab recovery, quota behavior, public release or whole-phase acceptance. Before production acceptance, use an isolated browser workspace to export/re-import v1, cancel/undo Upgrade, deliberately upgrade/save/reload, perform a complete replacement and export/import, check old-client refusal and stale-tab recovery, and inspect keyboard focus, Large/Plain rotation, Back and BFCache. Keep exact original/export hashes and actual storage outcomes.
+
 ## Preview and inspection
 
 The inspector shows saved/current and working-draft assets beside one another. Available views are native pixels, enlarged pixels, alpha, and field context. Transparency view maps alpha to grayscale. Geometry overlays show the occupied bounds, pivot, rotor envelopes, and nine-slice interior. Overlay markings are inspection aids, never baked into exported pixels.
